file tools/d/dayshelf_merge.sh the driver -- union, lift, reseat by stamp, and fall back on any shape it cannot read
file tools/fixtures/d/dayshelf_merge_control.sh 25 behaviors on real repositories, the fault reproduced under union from the failing side
file tools/fixtures/d/dayshelf_real_shelf_scan.sh the leg outside the pen -- the live shelf merged with itself
file tools/d/dayshelf_merge_witness.rish the rung; it also reads .gitattributes and this clone's config back
file .gitattributes merge=union leaves the day shelves; merge=dayshelf takes them, with the reason written where the elder reasoning stood
file tools/i/install_hooks.rish arms the driver by a relative path, so no host name enters git config
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the rung rostered tier lap beside index_row_bound
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front; the elder Bakery account shelved whole
file construction/archive/20260908-054012_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the elder account, as testimony

scope one lap: the day-shelf merge driver, its control, its live leg, its witness, the roster row, the arming, and the card.
status GREEN -- dayshelf_merge_witness GREEN on metal (25 pen behaviors, the live 37-row shelf byte-identical, the fault reproduced under union); install_hooks GREEN; QA 84/100/92/100, all B or better. Cold 187/183 green and hot 188/184 green, both tree_moved=no; the one red in each is standing_equipment's own live_group_plant pen leg, pre-existing on this pier and named in %549. Two hot reds of my own -- a letter-room misfile and a shelved link's depth -- were found and cured before the close.

recommend keep-going -- the six parked stashes are the honest next reach, standing_equipment_yield the largest.
